To determine the length of the hallway, we need to first find the speed of the robot in meters per second. The robot travels 1 kilometer in 9000 seconds. Since 1 kilometer is equal to 1000 meters, the speed of the robot is:

\[
\text{Speed} = \frac{1000 \text{ meters}}{9000 \text{ seconds}} = \frac{1000}{9000} = \frac{1}{9} \text{ meters per second}
\]

Next, we know that the robot takes 90 seconds to travel the length of the hallway. Using the speed we just calculated, we can find the length of the hallway by multiplying the speed by the time:

\[
\text{Length of the hallway} = \text{Speed} \times \text{Time} = \frac{1}{9} \text{ meters per second} \times 90 \text{ seconds} = \frac{90}{9} = 10 \text{ meters}
\]

Therefore, the length of the hallway is \(\boxed{10}\) meters.
